{#
  The dog-gear block (docs/DECISIONS.md 0013). Renders nothing while
  AMAZON_ASSOCIATE_TAG in site.py is empty (gear_links is then an empty list).
  Plain Amazon search links, never a product and never a home toxin test kit.
#}
{% if gear_links %}
<section class="gear" aria-labelledby="gear-heading">
  <h2 id="gear-heading">Dog gear for lake days</h2>
  <p>
    Heading to {{ water.name }} with your dog? These links search Amazon for
    dog gear. They point to search results, not to any one product. No gear
    changes what is in the water: keep your dog out of water that has an
    advisory on file, or that looks green, blue-green or scummy.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {% for g in gear_links %}
    <li><a href="{{ g.url }}" rel="{{ affiliate_rel }}">{{ g.label }}</a></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="muted" id="gear-disclosure">
    These are affiliate links: if you buy something after following one, this
    site earns a commission, and it costs you nothing extra.
    {{ amazon_disclosure }}
    {{ gear_endorsement }}
    <a href="{{ root }}privacy/#affiliate">More in the privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</section>
{% endif %}
